      "prompt": "STATE:\nShoes arrived two weeks late and in the wrong size. Also I see two charges of $120 on my card. What are you going to do about this?\n\nAnswer every question below about the STATE.\n\ndepartment (pick one option): Which team should handle this?\n  - returns: Exchanges, wrong or damaged items\n  - shipping: Delivery status, delays, lost packages\n  - billing: Charges, invoices, payment problems\n\nreturn_reason (pick one option): If the customer wants to return something, why?\n  - wrong_size: The item doesn't fit\n  - wrong_item: A different product was delivered\n  - damaged: The item arrived broken or faulty\n  - changed_mind: The item is fine, the customer no longer wants it\n  - other: A return reason that fits none of the above\n\nshipping_issue (pick one option): If this is a shipping problem, which kind is it?\n  - not_delivered: The package never arrived\n  - delayed: The package is late but still on its way\n  - wrong_address: The package went to the wrong place\n  - damaged_in_transit: The package arrived damaged\n  - other: A shipping problem that fits none of the above\n\nresolution (pick one option): What does the customer want to happen?\n  - exchange: Swap the item for a different one\n  - refund: Money back\n  - replacement: The same item sent again\n  - information: Just an answer, no action needed\n\ntone (pick one option): What is the customer's tone?\n  - calm\n  - frustrated\n  - angry\n\nReply with only a JSON object in exactly this shape. Replace every 0.0 with your number.\nnoul = the probability of yes. The probabilities of one question add up to 1.\nscore = the expected level: the sum of level × probability.\n{\"department\": {\"choice\": \"<option name>\", \"probabilities\": {\"returns\": 0.0, \"shipping\": 0.0, \"billing\": 0.0}}, \"return_reason\": {\"choice\": \"<option name>\", \"probabilities\": {\"wrong_size\": 0.0, \"wrong_item\": 0.0, \"damaged\": 0.0, \"changed_mind\": 0.0, \"other\": 0.0}}, \"shipping_issu